    21	## A11.1 What went wrong
    22	
    23	P3's assumption half (A1 §P3, `phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md:144-148`) requires the verification profile to record
    24	the *exact library and version, accepted signature encodings, public-key validation behavior, low-order-point
    25	handling, cofactor equation variant, and negative test vectors for each*. Two of those fields name concepts of
    26	Ed25519-style curves, which A1 used as its example (`:136`). V1 later registered OpenPGP P-256 and then, on
    27	2026-10-16, the hybrid ML-DSA-65 + P-256 (`formal/p8/HYBRID-REGISTRATION-RECORD.md`). Neither registration re-read the
    28	checklist.
    29	
    30	For ML-DSA, the two curve fields have no referent. The other four fields still apply in full. So the checklist
    31	names nothing specific to ML-DSA's own verification pitfalls: it **demands too little**. Nothing had been accepted
    32	on it. The assumption half was open (`formal/PROPERTIES.md:37`) and due after the freeze
    33	(`formal/freeze-v1/FREEZE-RECORD.md:81`).
    34	
    35	The method's defect: **a registered decision can change what an earlier registered sentence refers to, and nothing
    36	requires anyone to re-read that sentence.** §A11.4 adds that duty.
