     1	#!/usr/bin/env bash
     2	# Tessera V1 slot-2 policy signer: deployment (service/signer-gcp/README.md "Deploy"). OWNER DRAFT: not yet run.
     3	# Idempotent: every step checks for the resource first. Run the steps one at a time, in the order README.md "Deploy"
     4	# gives: `terraform apply` for the issuer falls between `role` and `job`, so there is no `all`.
     5	#
     6	#   service/signer-gcp/deploy.sh <step>
     7	#     sas | role | keyiam | registry | build | job | run-now | scheduler | harden | retire-instrument
     8	#
     9	# Inputs (environment), needed by `job` and `role`:
    10	#   REQUEST_QUEUE_URL, RESPONSE_QUEUE_URL   terraform output signer_queues (the "gpg" entry), service/issuer/infra
    11	#   FRAME_BUCKET                            terraform output result_bucket
    12	#   SIGN_UNTIL                              the window's signing stop: issuance-not-after minus 96 h, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ
    13	#
    14	# Scopes: GCP project tessera-slot2 (us-east1) and AWS account 477139661040 (profile tessera, us-east-2) only. Creates
    15	# no static credential: no AWS access keys and no GCP service-account keys. The signer reaches AWS by
    16	# AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity with a Google-issued ID token for its own service account, then AssumeRole into the
    17	# issuer's Terraform signer role (tessera-v1-issuer-signer-gpg), whose principal is the federated role made here.
