    29	4. For `LEDGER.md`, read the full relevant contract and combined-consequences table, not a single section. Translate each producer/consumer relation into which component supplies information and which relies on it.
    30	5. For every claimed cross-model join, identify the registered producer query and a broken companion whose mutation makes the consuming query fail. If severing the producer does not affect the consumer's registered query, call the relation complementary or capstone-internal rather than cross-model.
